<title>USA: Ag Dep't halts foreclosure sales for rights look.</title>
<headline>Ag Dep't halts foreclosure sales for rights look.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department will temporarily halt farm foreclosure sales so it can see if any civil rights violations were involved, Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Glickman said he hoped the review would be complete by February 1, 1997. An aide said about 100 sales, the result of delinquent loans, were involved. Twenty cases involved minority-group farmers, she said.</p>
</text>
